user.description:
The Amazon helper on your Zima box signs in with a real hidden browser and reads your Your Orders page now and then (one page, last 30 days), so the Orders screen shows exact product names and photos. What you type here is passed once to that helper and kept only on Zima; Home Assistant keeps just a pairing key.

Authenticator key: the text key Amazon shows when you add an authenticator app (Login & security > 2-Step Verification > Add new app > "Can't scan the barcode?"). With it, the helper can sign in again by itself. Leave it empty to type a 6-digit code instead.

